---
title: Focaccia di Recco
servings: 8
yield: 2 focacce, 12 inches each
tags: [italian, vegetarian]
cuisine: italian
time: 1 hour 45 minutes
source: Focaccia di Recco al Formaggio by Marie Roffey, Sugar Salt Magic, https://www.sugarsaltmagic.com/focaccia-di-recco
---

Set aside 2 teaspoons of the @extra virgin olive oil{1/4%cup} for the tops.

In a #large bowl{}, stir the @water{1%cup}, the rest of the oil, the
@sea salt{2%tsp}(fine) and the @bread flour{390%g} together with a spoon.

Knead on a lightly floured counter ~{10%minutes}, until smooth and elastic. Add
flour only if it sticks badly. Wrap it and rest at room temperature ~{1%hour}.

Heat the oven to 250°C (480°F; 230°C fan) and lightly oil two
#12-inch pizza trays{}.

Cut the dough into 4 pieces and keep 3 covered. Roll one out as thin as you
can, about 14 to 15 inches across and 1 mm or less. Lay it over a tray so it
hangs over the edge.

Dot half the @stracchino{500%g}(or crescenza) over it in small pieces.

Roll a second piece just as thin and lay it over the cheese. Press the edges
together around the rim, trim off the excess and crimp.

Brush the top with some of the reserved oil, tear 4 or 5 small holes with your
fingers so steam can escape, and sprinkle with a little @sea salt{}.

Make the second focaccia the same way with the remaining dough and cheese.

Bake ~{15%minutes} to 18 minutes, until golden with some darker blisters. Cut
and eat straight away.

> The dough should be thin enough to see the counter through. If it springs
> back while rolling, rest it a few minutes and go again.
